== Retiring members ==
The seats of [[Division of Hinkler|Hinkler]] (Queensland) and [[Division of Maribyrnong|Maribyrnong]] (Victoria) were vacant at the time the federal election was called, following the resignation of [[Keith Pitt]] (Nationals) and [[Bill Shorten]] (Labor) on 19 and 20 January 2025 respectively. No by-elections were held for the seats due to their proximity to the general election.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-01-23/by-election-unlikely-for-hinkler-seat-after-pitt-resignation/104750828|first=Nikki|last=Sorbello|title=By-election unlikely for Hinkler seat after Keith Pitt officially resigns|publisher=ABC News|date=23 January 2025|access-date=23 January 2025|archive-date=22 January 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122221147/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-01-23/by-election-unlikely-for-hinkler-seat-after-pitt-resignation/104750828|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite press release|via=Ministers for the Department of Social Services|url=https://ministers.dss.gov.au/media-releases/17341|title=Statement from the Hon. Bill Shorten MP, Minister for the NDIS and Government Services and Member for Maribyrnong|publisher=The Hon Bill Shorten MP|date=16 January 2025|access-date=18 January 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250118111920/https://ministers.dss.gov.au/media-releases/17341|archive-date=18 January 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

