* {{flag|Singapore}}: Prime Minister [[Lawrence Wong]] wrote a letter to congratulate Albanese for his victory, stating that both countries are like-minded partners with a common interest in upholding an open, inclusive and rules-based global order.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=Prime Minister and Minister for Finance Lawrence Wong's Congratulatory Telephone Calls with Foreign Leaders, 5 May 2025 |url=https://www.mfa.gov.sg/Newsroom/Press-Statements-Transcripts-and-Photos/2025/05/20250505-PM-Congrats-Calls |access-date=6 May 2025 |publisher=Ministry of Foreign Affairs |location=Singapore |url-status=live |archive-date=6 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506124502/https://www.mfa.gov.sg/Newsroom/Press-Statements-Transcripts-and-Photos/2025/05/20250505-PM-Congrats-Calls |language=en}}</ref> Albanese replied with his own congratulatory message to Wong for winning the [[2025 Singaporean general election]], which was held concurrently on the same day.<ref>{{cite news|title=GE2025: PM Wong receives congratulatory calls from foreign leaders on election victory |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/politics/ge2025-pm-wong-receives-congratulatory-calls-from-foreign-leaders-on-election-victory|work=[[The Straits Times]]|location=Singapore|date=6 May 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250505171759/https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/politics/ge2025-pm-wong-receives-congratulatory-calls-from-foreign-leaders-on-election-victory|archive-date=5 May 2025|url-status=live|access-date=6 May 2025|last=Raguraman|first=Anjali}}</ref>
* {{flag|Spain}}: Prime Minister [[Pedro Sánchez]] congratulated Albanese and the Labor Party on social media stating that Australia and Spain would continue working together for social justice and the defense of common values.<ref>{{cite tweet |number=1918648087863550385 |user=sanchezcastejon |title=Enhorabuena @AlboMP y al Partido Laborista por vuestra clara victoria en las elecciones de hoy. |trans-title=Congratulations @AlboMP and the Labor Party for your clear victory in today's elections. |quote=Te deseo el mayor éxito en este nuevo mandato. Australia y España seguiremos trabajando juntos por la justicia social y en defensa de nuestros valores comunes. |first=Pedro |last=Sánchez |date=3 May 2025 |access-date=4 May 2025 |url-status=live |archive-date=4 May 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250504123741/https://x.com/sanchezcastejon/status/1918648087863550385}}</ref>
* {{flag|Taiwan}}: President [[Lai Ching-te]] congratulated Albanese on his election win while also praising Taiwan's positive relationship with Australia.<ref>{{cite tweet |number=1918880061513441517 |access-date=5 May 2025 |date=4 May 2025 |title=Sincere congratulations to @AlboMP on your election win. |quote=#Taiwan cherishes its enduring relationship with #Australia, grounded in our commitment to shared values & our robust economic ties. I look forward to deepening our partnership further to promote a free & open Indo-Pacifc. |url-status=live |archive-date=5 May 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250505034442/https://x.com/ChingteLai/status/1918880061513441517 |user=ChingteLai |first=Lai |last=Ching-te}}</ref>
* {{flag|Tibet}}: Sikyong [[Penpa Tsering]] congratulated Albanese and applauded his compassion for Tibetan refugees.<ref>{{cite web |publisher=Central Tibetan Administration |access-date=6 May 2025 |title=Sikyong Penpa Tsering Congratulates Australian Prime Minister Anthony Norman Albanese on His Re-election |date=5 May 2025 |location=Dharamshala |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506014216/https://tibet.net/sikyong-penpa-tsering-congratulates-australian-prime-minister-anthony-norman-albanese-on-his-re-election/ |url=https://tibet.net/sikyong-penpa-tsering-congratulates-australian-prime-minister-anthony-norman-albanese-on-his-re-election/ |url-status=live |archive-date=6 May 2025}}</ref>
* {{flag|Ukraine}}: President [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]] congratulated Albanese on his electoral victory and wished him continued success in serving the people of Australia and delivering meaningful achievements.<ref>{{cite tweet |number=1918662599677288614 |user=ZelenskyyUa |title=Congratulations to Prime Minister @AlboMP on a confident electoral victory. I wish you continued success in serving the people of Australia and delivering meaningful achievements. |quote=Ukraine sincerely values Australia's unwavering support and its principled stance on ending Russia's war and securing a dignified and lasting peace. We look forward to further strengthening our productive partnership in pursuit of peace, security, and freedom. |first=Volodymyr |last=Zelenskyy |date=3 May 2025 |access-date=3 May 2025 |url-status=live |archive-date=4 May 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250504061528/https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1918662599677288614}}</ref>
* {{flag|United Kingdom}}: Prime Minister [[Keir Starmer]] congratulated Albanese on social media, saying that "long distance friendships can be the strongest" and looked forward to "continue to work together" on shared ambitions.<ref>{{cite news |date=3 May 2025 |title=Starmer congratulates Albanese on re-election, hailing UK-Australia friendship |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/keir-starmer-peter-dutton-anthony-albanese-australia-labour-party-b2744302.html |access-date=3 May 2025 |website=[[The Independent]] |first=Helen |last=Corbett |url-status=live |archive-date=3 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250503171155/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/keir-starmer-peter-dutton-anthony-albanese-australia-labour-party-b2744302.html}}</ref>
* {{flag|United States}}: Secretary of State [[Marco Rubio]] congratulated Albanese on his electoral victory, saying that he is looking forward to "deepening its relationship with Australia to advance our common interests and promote freedom and stability in the Indo-Pacific and globally."<ref>{{cite press release |first=Marco |last=Rubio |author2=Secretary of State |date=3 May 2025 |title=Australian Federal Election |url=https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2025/05/australian-federal-election/ |access-date=4 May 2025|publisher=United States Department of State |url-status=live |archive-date=4 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250504063127/https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2025/05/australian-federal-election/ |language=en-US}}</ref> President Trump later congratulated Albanese and told journalists after disembarking [[Marine One]] that he is fond of Albanese, and said that he has a good relationship with Albanese and that he knew nothing about the opposition. In this press conference regarding the call, Albanese stated, "We'll continue to engage."<ref>{{cite news |work=The Sydney Morning Herald |url-access=subscription |url=https://www.smh.com.au/world/north-america/trump-praises-albanese-says-he-has-no-idea-who-opponent-was-in-australian-election-20250505-p5lwlo.html |access-date=5 May 2025 |date=5 May 2025 |first=Michael |last=Koziol |title=Trump calls Albanese after saying he had 'no idea' who PM's opponent was in election |location=Washington |url-status=live |archive-date=5 May 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250505033514/https://www.smh.com.au/world/north-america/trump-praises-albanese-says-he-has-no-idea-who-opponent-was-in-australian-election-20250505-p5lwlo.html}}</ref>

==== Organisations ====
* {{flag|European Union}}: President of the European Commission [[Ursula von der Leyen]] congratulated Albanese and his party on their victory in the Australian federal election.<ref>{{cite tweet |url-status=live |archive-date=4 May 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250504063535/https://x.com/vonderleyen/status/1918639779228377520 |number=1918639779228377520 |user=vonderleyen |title=Congratulations to @AlboMP and his party on their victory in the Australian federal election. |quote=Europeans and Australians are not just friends – we're mates. Let us seize this moment of stability to deepen our cooperation. Together, we can expand trade, investment and work to promote our shared democratic values and a free, open Indo-Pacific. |first=Ursula |last=von der Leyen |date=3 May 2025 |access-date=3 May 2025}}</ref>

==== Individuals ====
* [[Dalai Lama]]: The [[14th Dalai Lama]] wrote to Albanese to congratulate him on his re-election as Prime Minister following his party's victory and expressed his "deep gratitude to the Australian government and its people for their interest in and support for the Tibetan people's freedom and dignity".<ref>{{cite web |date=4 May 2025 |title=His Holiness the Dalai Lama Offers Congratulations to Anthony Albanese on His Re-election as Prime Minister of Australia |publisher=[[Central Tibetan Administration]] |url=https://tibet.net/his-holiness-the-dalai-lama-offers-congratulations-to-anthony-albanese-on-his-re-election-as-prime-minister-of-australia/ |url-status=live |archive-date=6 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506014044/https://tibet.net/his-holiness-the-dalai-lama-offers-congratulations-to-anthony-albanese-on-his-re-election-as-prime-minister-of-australia/ |location=Dharamshala |access-date=5 May 2025}}</ref>

